silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_24_rosetta_stone_cross_domain_sections_06_six_step_scaffold_exposition_concrete_anchor_9#cat silm:hasLongDescription "The Cat is the most general class source leg shared by all five domain readings. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Cat', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
